---
import EbookPrint from '../../layouts/EbookPrint.astro';
import ReferenceCover from '../../components/ebook/ReferenceCover.astro';
import OrientationChapter from '../../components/ebook/OrientationChapter.astro';
---
<EbookPrint title="Reference Companion — Spread 1 Preview">
  <div class="spread-frame">
    <div class="spread-page">
      <ReferenceCover
        title="Quranic Grammar Reference Companion"
        subtitle="A Quick-Reference Kit for Classical Arabic"
        brand="Quranic Grammar"
        volume="Volume Three"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="spread-page">
      <OrientationChapter number="01" title="Every Word Is a Noun, Verb, or Particle. Nothing Else.">
        <p>Seven rules. Ninety percent of the Quran. Keep this orientation close while you study — each principle is a cheat-code that unlocks a whole category of meaning.</p>
        <p><strong>The rule:</strong> Every Arabic word — no exceptions — belongs to one of three categories: <strong>ism</strong> (noun), <strong>fiʿl</strong> (verb), or <strong>ḥarf</strong> (particle).</p>
        <p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Once you know what <em>kind</em> of word you're reading, every other rule becomes easier — because rules apply to types, not random words.</p>
        <p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>ٱللَّهُ</strong> — noun (names Allah)</li>
          <li><strong>كَتَبَ</strong> — verb (he wrote — past time)</li>
          <li><strong>فِي</strong> — particle (in — meaningless without what follows)</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Cheat shortcut:</strong> If a word has <strong>ال</strong> or <strong>tanween</strong>, it is definitely a noun. If it has a tense prefix (يَ, تَ, نَ, أَ), it is definitely a verb.</p>
      </OrientationChapter>
    </div>
  </div>
</EbookPrint>

<style is:global>
  html, body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: #0a0b0d;
  }
  .spread-frame {
    width: 1200px;
    height: 1500px;
    background: #0a0b0d;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .spread-page {
    width: 528px;
    height: 816px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55), 0 0 0 1px #1c1e24;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #0f1115;
  }
  /* Neutralize page-break rules inside the preview frame so two
     pages sit side by side instead of forcing print breaks. */
  .spread-page .ebook-page,
  .spread-page section.ebook-page,
  .spread-page .cover {
    page-break-after: auto !important;
    break-after: auto !important;
  }
</style>
